      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Subject: Inquiry Regarding Original Charter and Claim to Sovereign Succession Rights Pertaining to the House of Valerius and the Principality of San Michele\n\n\nDear Sir/Madam,\n\n\nI hope this letter finds you well. I am writing to bring to your attention an important historical matter concerning the succession of the principality of San Michele and the family of Valerius.\n\n\nI am the present claimant to the estate as a direct descendent of the original sovereign, as evidenced by original documentation, including the authentic charter I possess, which was signed in the latter part of the 19th century. Due to the tumult following the 1922 dissolution of the principality, some members of my lineage chose to hide these documents to preserve their integrity and prevent their potential misuse. I am here to submit these documents, fully authenticated, to establish the legally recognized continuity of my family's sovereign lineage.\n\n\nThis matter transcends a mere historical interest and delves into the matter of authentic sovereign succession, different from mere entitlement to heirlooms or property. With conscientiousness in mind, I hereby assert my request for the Italian Ministry of Foreign Affairs' support in recognizing and validating my succession rights in accordance with international historical precedents and family documentation.\n\n\nI am prepared to work",
